    "module":  "respiratory",
    "category":  "disease",
    "description":  "Acute respiratory failure (ARF) is a life-threatening condition in which the respiratory system cannot maintain adequate gas exchange, defined as PaO2 \u003c60 mmHg (Type 1, hypoxaemic) or PaCO2 \u003e50 mmHg with acidosis (Type 2, hypercapnic). Type 1 (hypoxaemic) failure occurs in conditions causing V/Q mismatch or shunt: pneumonia, pulmonary oedema, ARDS, pulmonary embolism. Type 2 (hypercapnic) failure occurs when ventilatory drive or muscle strength is insufficient: COPD exacerbation, neuromuscular disease, severe asthma, obesity hypoventilation. ARF is a medical emergency requiring immediate assessment and intervention including supplemental oxygen, non-invasive ventilation, or intubation.",
